.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt QUARK_QUEUE_GET_STATS 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm quark_queue_get_stats
.Nd fetch queue statistics
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In quark.h
.Ft void
.Fn quark_queue_get_stats "struct quark_queue *qq" "struct quark_queue_stats *qs"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
copies out all internal statistics from
.Fa qq
into
.Fa qs .
.Vt quark_queue_stats
is defined as:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct quark_queue_stats {
	u64	insertions;
	u64	removals;
	u64	aggregations;
	u64	non_aggregations;
	u64	lost;
	u64	garbage_collections;
	u64	bpf_state_lost;
	u64	bpf_metadata_lost;
	u64	bpf_retprobe_missed;
	u64	stalls;
	int	bpf_retprobe_stats_valid;
	int	backend;
};
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "non_aggregations"
.It Em insertions
A counter of all events that were inserted into the queue
sorting/buffering structures, this is roughly 1:1 with the actual events we read
from the backend.
.It Em removals
A counter of removals of the above, you can count alive items by
counting the difference.
.It Em aggregations
A counter of how many events were aggregated, this is an absolute
counter, meaning a FORK+EXEC+EXIT counts as 1 aggregation, which consumes 3
events.
.It Em non_aggregations
The opposite of
.Em aggregations .
It is increased by one when we didn't aggregate.
.It Em lost
A counter of missed backend events.
This can happen if the user didn't call
.Xr quark_queue_get_event 3
fast enough or if
.Em quark
simply can't handle the load, the former is way more likely.
It is a state counter representing total loss, the user should compare to an old
reading to know if it increased.
.It Em garbage_collections
A counter of cached objects (processes, sockets and pods) that were
deleted after expiring their grace time.
.It Em bpf_state_lost
Discarded or rejected BPF invocation frames: bounded-depth or map exhaustion,
missed-return recovery, task exit with pending state, or ambiguous metadata.
Includes ignored commands used to track nesting, so it is not an exact count
of lost emitted events.
.It Em bpf_metadata_lost
Operations with a failed copied-attribute read or a successful load without
captured program identity.
The operation event can still be delivered with the corresponding validity bit clear.
.It Em bpf_retprobe_missed
Tracefs return-probe misses, separate from ring-buffer loss.
May overlap recovered frames in
.Em bpf_state_lost ;
do not sum these as a count of distinct missing events.
Older kernels omit return-instance-pool exhaustion from tracefs profiles.
These counters can undercount losses and are not proof of complete capture.
.It Em bpf_retprobe_stats_valid
Nonzero if the last tracefs miss-count refresh succeeded with BPF telemetry
enabled; otherwise the miss count is unavailable or stale.
.It Em stalls
A counter of perf rings that are stalled due to corrupt records.
A stalled ring is abandoned and no further events are read from it.
Only meaningful on the
.Dv QQ_KPROBE
backend, zero on
.Dv QQ_EBPF .
.It Em backend
Active queue backend, either
.Dv QQ_EBPF
or
.Dv QQ_KPROBE .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
